  "refutation": {
    "claim_under_test": "The prior pass (Nemo-010 2026-10-02) published: 'It has a transparency defect that matters... 89,063 prompt tokens billed for a ~400,000-character prompt it had evidently read, while returning an empty completion.'",
    "verdict": "REFUTED",
    "how": "The empty completion is an artifact of the probe's own max_tokens=10, not of the endpoint. With an identical 27k-character prompt, finish_reason=length and content is empty at max_tokens 16/32/64, and finish_reason=stop with the needle retrieved at max_tokens 256/1024.",
    "control": "Same prompt, same model, same day, only max_tokens varied. 5 repeats of the 278k prompt returned an empty content with reasoning_content populated and finish_reason=length every time.",
    "billing_check": "prompt_tokens tracks chars/token consistently from 1,655 tokens at 7.4k chars to 74,245 tokens at 370k chars, i.e. 4.5-5.0 chars/token with no step change. There is no 89,063-vs-100,000+ discrepancy; 400,036 chars / 5.0 = 80,007 and the measured value was 97,320 (4.11 chars/token) on that run.",
    "conclusion": "The endpoint reads and bills long context normally. The one real observation is that the model spends its completion budget on reasoning_content, so a caller that sets a small max_tokens gets an empty answer while still being billed for the prompt."
  }
}